{
  "tema": 7032,
  "slug": "a-mi-me-gusta",
  "titulo": "Repeating the indirect pronoun with verbs like gustar",
  "subtitulo": "A mí me gusta, a María le encanta.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "With gustar-type verbs, the short pronoun (me, te, le, nos, les) is required. The a + pronoun or a + person (a mí, a María) is optional and adds emphasis or clarity, but can never replace the short pronoun.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs like **gustar**, **encantar**, **interesar**, **molestar**, **fascinar**, **aburrir**, **apasionar** take an indirect object: the person who feels it."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **short pronoun** (**me, te, le, nos, les**) is **always required**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**A** + pronoun (**a mí, a ti, a él, a ella, a usted, a nosotros, a ellos, a ustedes**) is **optional**. It emphasizes, contrasts or clarifies, but it can't stand alone."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "(a mí)",
            "+ me +",
            "gusta..."
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The same goes when you name the person: **a María le**, **a mi papá le**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **a mí** is the spotlight; **me** is the actor. The show can go on without the spotlight, never without the actor."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==A mí me== gusta mucho el mole.",
              "en": "I really like mole."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==A ti te== gustan las carreras de caballos?",
              "en": "Do you like horse racing?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==A ella== no ==le== gusta el pozole.",
              "en": "She doesn't like pozole."
            },
            {
              "es": "==A él le== molesta mucho el ruido del tráfico.",
              "en": "Traffic noise really bothers him."
            },
            {
              "es": "==A ellos les== aburre el tenis.",
              "en": "Tennis bores them."
            },
            {
              "es": "==A nosotros nos== apasionan los carros de carreras.",
              "en": "We're passionate about race cars."
            },
            {
              "es": "==A María le== encantan las películas de los cincuenta.",
              "en": "María loves movies from the fifties."
            },
            {
              "es": "==A mi papá le== fascinan los carros antiguos.",
              "en": "My dad is crazy about vintage cars."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
